WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.060
MFA enrollment is the process of binding an authenticator or factor to an account or identity.

2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:12.360
It is security-sensitive because whoever controls enrollment controls future proof of identity.

3
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:19.980
The user should be appropriately verified before adding a factor, and enrollment endpoints should require protection equal to the risk of the account.

4
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.680
A logged-in session may not be enough for high-risk enrollment; step-up verification may be appropriate.

5
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.120
Enrollment should confirm factor possession.

6
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:35.900
The application or identity provider should not merely record that a factor was requested; it should verify that the user can complete the challenge.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.560
MFA metadata should be stored safely and should contain only what is needed: factor type, enrollment state, display name or device label, timestamps, recovery status, and other operational context.

8
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:56.500
Avoid storing unnecessary secrets or sensitive authenticator material in application logs or broad-access tables.

9
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.940
Many accounts need more than one factor, because devices are lost, replaced, or upgraded.

10
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.640
Supporting multiple factors can improve availability, but it also increases management complexity.

11
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.700
Device naming helps users recognize their authenticators.

12
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.680
Factor replacement should require appropriate proof.

13
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:22.300
Administrative enrollment is especially risky because support staff may be able to change future access without the user's normal factor.

14
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.620
User notifications are a valuable control.

15
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:33.080
When a factor is added, removed, reset, or renamed, users should receive clear notice through an appropriate channel.

16
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.860
Notifications are not a substitute for secure controls, but they improve visibility and response.

17
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:47.600
Treat enrollment and factor reset as seriously as login because a weak enrollment path can become the easiest way to defeat otherwise strong MFA.
